{"@context":{"lean":"lean:","block":"block:","imports":{"@type":"@id"}},"@graph":[{"@id":"lean:module:QOU.Eightfold.PointwiseAgreementOnReduced","@type":"LeanModule","name":"QOU.Eightfold.PointwiseAgreementOnReduced","imports":["lean:module:Init","lean:module:Mathlib.RingTheory.Nilpotent.Lemmas","lean:module:Mathlib.RingTheory.Ideal.Quotient.Defs","lean:module:Mathlib.Data.ZMod.Basic"],"declarations":4,"chunks":1},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Eightfold.PointwiseAgreementOnReduced.twoNilpotentZModFour","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Eightfold.PointwiseAgreementOnReduced.twoNilpotentZModFour","kind":"theorem","line":77,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Eightfold/PointwiseAgreementOnReduced.lean#L77-L80","doc":"A concrete non-reduced witness, so the sharpness theorem is not vacuous: `(2 : ZMod 4)`\nis nonzero and nilpotent, hence lies in every prime ideal while differing from `0`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Eightfold.PointwiseAgreementOnReduced.exists_ne_of_not_isReduced","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Eightfold.PointwiseAgreementOnReduced.exists_ne_of_not_isReduced","kind":"theorem","line":65,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Eightfold/PointwiseAgreementOnReduced.lean#L65-L75","doc":"**Sharpness: reducedness cannot be dropped.**  In any non-reduced ring there are two\nDISTINCT elements agreeing modulo every prime -- invisible to every point of the spectrum.\nSo a pointwise check, however exhaustive, does not by itself give equality. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Eightfold.PointwiseAgreementOnReduced.eq_of_apply_sub_mem_all_primes","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Eightfold.PointwiseAgreementOnReduced.eq_of_apply_sub_mem_all_primes","kind":"theorem","line":58,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Eightfold/PointwiseAgreementOnReduced.lean#L58-L63","doc":"**Pointwise agreement is equality, for a reduced target.**  Two maps into a reduced ring\nwhose values agree modulo every prime are equal as maps.  This is the shape the objection\ntakes: the conclusion is an identity of maps, not a list of coincidences. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Eightfold.PointwiseAgreementOnReduced.eq_of_sub_mem_all_primes","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Eightfold.PointwiseAgreementOnReduced.eq_of_sub_mem_all_primes","kind":"theorem","line":46,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Eightfold/PointwiseAgreementOnReduced.lean#L46-L56","doc":"In a reduced ring, an element lying in **every** prime ideal is zero -- so two elements\nagreeing modulo every prime are equal.  This is the algebraic content of \"pointwise\nagreement is equality\". ","signatureChunk":0}]}